Good point Stan, we should fix that.<br><br>By the way, we have been improving COLLADA Physics support for upcoming Bullet 2.67 version.<br><br>It will be possible to take an arbitrary Bullet dynamics world, attach the ColladaConverter and export a snapshot to .dae.<br>It supports collision geometry, rigidbodies and generic 6dof constraints. So you can use Bullet API to create COLLADA Physics content, without needing to digg into the COLLADA DOM etc.<br><br>I haven't played with this feature yet, my collegue wrote it. It would be nice to add 'export .dae' and 'import .dae' buttons in the Bullet demos.<br><br>It should help with debugging and reproducing problems, without having access to the full source code.<br><br>Thanks,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Wed Feb 06, 2008 7:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
